<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch10-double-integrals" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Double Integrals</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>A double integral adds contributions over a plane region. We begin with rectangular sums, then use iterated integrals to compute them on regions described by slices. Polar coordinates provide a first geometric substitution rule. Throughout, ordinary area is nonnegative; an oriented area form records an additional choice of orientation.</p>
  </introduction>

